# Example events/*.json bridge target — see events/example_fancy_join_message.json.
#
# Demonstrates PlayerJoinWrapper's join_message get/set pair. The generic BukkitEvent wrapper could
# technically reach this too (event.get("joinMessage")/event.set("joinMessage", ...)), but that
# round-trips through Adventure's Component type reflectively on every read/write — miss the exact
# accessor Bukkit expects and it either throws or silently no-ops, and the raw Component would need
# manual serialization before a script could do anything useful with it. PlayerJoinWrapper's
# join_message property is already a plain MiniMessage-parseable string on the way in and out, so a
# script never touches Component internals at all.
#
# Setting an empty string suppresses the default broadcast entirely (see setJoinMessage's javadoc);
# this instead rewrites it with the player's own name still substituted in via Player.name — the
# join event fires with Player already bound, same as every other player-shaped event.
def on_join():
    event.set_join_message("<gray>[<gold>+</gold>] <yellow>" + Player.name + "<gray> stepped onto the server.")
end
